Z||000003||Shaun41178||05-21-99||03:11 PM||||You guys want to know something interesting?<p>GM made a 325 hp (more?) twin turbo 3.0 liter v6 and put it in a Beretta.  This was in the early 90's to see if it could be some type of replacement for the F-body platform.<p>Needless to say it didn't go into production but if anyone knows anyone high up in the GM corporate or Special Vehicles Division then I am sure there are still some info on it.  Perhaps like part numbers and stuff?!!  It would be a great way to go out and build a awesome engine when they have all the parts listed and how they did it.  Plus it was in a Beretta so i am sure that everythign could fit in a Fiero as well.<p>This car was in a Hot Rod issue.  Just check the last two years between 96-98.  It is there somewhere.  In fact I am going to go to the library now to see if I can find it.  Since I know what I am loking for it shouldn't be too hard to find.  hopefully it is still there and if I find it I will post the issue here.
Z||000004||SCCA FIERO||05-21-99||04:08 PM||||Lemma know if you find the issue. Keep us posted....
Z||000005||Eric||05-21-99||04:43 PM||||There was a V6 turbo trans am in limited production in the late 80s.  It and some other trans ams were featured on Car and Driver TV on TNN last Sunday.  They said the car was underated at 250 hp.  The car really made over 350 hp. It was the fastest trans am ever, 0-60 in 4.6 seconds.  The only car ever to not need modification to be the pace car for the Indy 500.<p>The GMC typhoon and syclone were turbo V6s too.  I think these trucks had a displacement of over 4 liters, but to my knowledge, they also were pushrods.  They were rated at 250 hp as I recall, but they got to 60 in about 5 seconds flat.  I saw a syclone go from a standing start to out of sight in the blink of an eye a few years back and now I wonder what turbo V6 in my car would be like.<p>Does anyone know the displacement of the "stock block"  old early 90s V6 pushrod indy cars had?  Those things were always contenders for the pole at Indianapolis. 
Z||000006||SCCA FIERO||05-21-99||06:17 PM||||In 1989 Pontiac installed the Gran National motor in it's 20th anniversary T/A. It is a 3.8 Turbo. In 91 GMC put a turbo 4.3 in the Syclones and Typhoons. They made 280hp and were intercooled. Both of these mills are pushrod engines.
Z||000007||Shaun41178||05-22-99||12:00 AM||||ok race fans i found the issue.<p>It is the June 98 issue.  It is not 320 hp it is 385 from a 3.3 liter.  twin turbo engine.  Forged rods, forged crank and forged pistons roller rockers and running on 16 psi of boost.  All too cool if you ask me oh yea and has an intercooler. <p>Plus in the same issue there are 200 hp 2.8 liters.  and it mentions that the engines had roller cams.  I wonder how they did that unless the heads were aluminum
